.TH SDL_GetRectEnclosingPointsFloat 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetRectEnclosingPointsFloat \- Calculate a minimal rectangle enclosing a set of points with float precision.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_rect.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetRectEnclosingPointsFloat(const SDL_FPoint *points, int count, const SDL_FRect *clip, SDL_FRect *result);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If
.BR clip
is not NULL then only points inside of the clipping rectangle are considered\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I points
an array of
.BR SDL_FPoint
structures representing points to be enclosed\[char46]
.TP
.I count
the number of structures in the
.BR points
array\[char46]
.TP
.I clip
an
.BR SDL_FRect
used for clipping or NULL to enclose all points\[char46]
.TP
.I result
an
.BR SDL_FRect
structure filled in with the minimal enclosing rectangle\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if any points were enclosed or false if all the points were outside of the clipping rectangle\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

